hadiths[80]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3004","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and said: 'I came to you last night, but nothing prevented me from entering the house you were in except that there was a statue of a man in the house, and there was a curtain screen in the house containing images. So order that the head of the statue be cut off so that it becomes like the form of a tree, and order that the screen be cut up.' In another narration: 'There is a screen in the house on the wall in which there are images, so cut off their heads and make them into a floor covering or cushions to be trodden upon, for we do not enter a house in which there are images.' So they were made into two cushions that were trodden upon. 'And order that the dog be taken out.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) did so, and the dog turned out to be a puppy belonging to Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) under a shelf of theirs."" He said: ""He kept enjoining the good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought—or I saw—that he would make him an heir."""
"3005","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: Abu al-Qasim, peace be upon him, said: ""Take them both off together or put them both on together. When you put on, begin with the right, and when you take off, begin with the left."
"3006","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saw a boy whose hair had been partly shaved and partly left, so he forbade them from that and said: ""Shave it all or leave it all."
"3007","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""When one of you applies kohl, let him apply it an odd number of times, and when he uses stones for cleaning, let him use them an odd number of times."
"3008","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, elevated to the Prophet: ""When you put on your sandals, begin with the right, and when you take them off, begin with the left. Let the right be the first to be put on and the left the last to be taken off. Do not walk in one sandal; take them both off or put them both on."
"3009","[AI-translation] From Sharid, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saw a man dragging his lower garment and hastened toward him or trotted toward him, and said: ""Raise your garment and fear Allah."" He said: ""I am bowlegged and my knees knock together."" So he said: ""Raise your garment, for all of the creation of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is beautiful."" That man was not seen afterwards except that his garment reached the middle of his shins or to the middle of his shins."
"3010","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Honor the hair."
"3011","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, saw a white garment on 'Umar and said: ""Is this garment of yours new or washed?"" He said: ""Rather, washed."" And in a narration: ""new,"" so he said: ""Wear new clothes, live a praised life, and die a martyr."
"3012","[AI-translation] Rahman al-Juhshi that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to Abu Qatada: ""If you have hair, then honor it."
"3013","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Dharr from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: ""The best things with which to dye this gray hair are henna and katam."
"3014","[AI-translation] Husayn, elevated to the Prophet: ""Verily, when Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant."
"3015","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah, 'Azza wa Jall, when He bestows a blessing upon a servant, loves to see the effect of His blessing upon him. He dislikes misery and appearing miserable, and He hates the persistent beggar, and loves the chaste, modest, and self-reliant."
"3016","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said: ""Verily, Allah does not look at the one who lets his lower garment hang down."
"3017","[AI-translation] dyed garments and said: ""Verily, these are from the garments of the disbelievers, so do not wear them."
"3018","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had a ring made and had an engraving put on it. He said: ""We have had a ring made and engraved an engraving in it, so let no one engrave upon its engraving."" Then Anas said: ""It is as if I can see its gleam on his hand."
"3019","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Sawdah went out after the verse of hijāb was revealed, to attend to her need. She was a large woman who could not go unrecognized by anyone who knew her. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb saw her and said: “O Sawdah! By Allah, you cannot hide from us, so consider how you go out.” She said: So she turned back, returning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in my house, dining, and in his hand was a bone (with meat on it). She entered and said: “O Messenger of Allah! I went out for some need of mine, and ʿUmar said to me such and such.” She said: Then Allah sent revelation to him, then the revelation was lifted from him, while the bone was still in his hand—he had not put it down. He said: “Indeed, permission has been given to you to go out for your needs.” And in a narration: “for your needs (plural).”"
"3020","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Umar said: The Magians were mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), and he said: ""They let their mustaches grow long and shave their beards, so differ from them."" Ibn 'Umar used to cut his mustache as a sheep or camel is sheared."
"3021","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Mu'adh bin Jabal: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he said: ""Beware of luxury! For the servants of Allah are not those who live luxuriously."
"3022","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Mu'awiyah, elevated to the Prophet: ""Any woman who adds to her hair the hair of another, she is only adding falsehood."
"3023","[AI-translation] From Anas, elevated: The izar is to half the shin, but when he saw the severity of that upon the Muslims, he said: To the ankles. There is no good in what is below that."
"3024","[AI-translation] From Kurayb, he said: I was leading Ibn Abbas in the alley of Abu Lahab, and that was after his sight had gone. He said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""While a man was in his garment, looking at his sides, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he continues sinking into it until the Day of Resurrection."
"3025","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Simplicity is part of faith, meaning austerity."
"3026","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas from the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: ""Three whom the angels do not approach: the one in a state of major ritual impurity, the drunkard, and the one smeared with khaluq."
"3027","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said what he said regarding trailing the hem, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about us? He said: ""Trail it a handspan."" Umm Salamah said: Then the two feet will be uncovered. He said: ""Then trail it a cubit."
"3028","[AI-translation] Aslamiyyah, she said: Some women from among the people of Sham entered upon Aisha. Aisha said: Where are you from? They said: From the people of Hims. She said: The companions of the bathhouses? They said: Yes. Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""The bathhouse is forbidden for the women of my ummah."" A woman among them said: But I have daughters, may I comb their hair with this drink? She said: What drink? She said: Wine! Aisha said: Would you be pleased to comb your hair with the blood of a pig? She said: No. She said: For it is like it."
"3029","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah from the Prophet, peace be upon him: The hem of a woman is a handspan. She said: I said: Then her feet will be exposed? He said: A cubit, let them not add to it."
"3030","[AI-translation] From Zayd bin Arqam, elevated: ""Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my ummah, forbidden for its males."
"3031","[AI-translation] From Ikrimah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas, when he put on his izar, he would lower the front of his izar until its edges fell upon the back of his feet, and he would raise the izar from behind him. He said: I said to him: Why do you wear the izar like this? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, wearing the izar in this manner."
"3032","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr, elevated: ""The master of the fragrant herbs of the people of Paradise is henna."
"3033","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (peace be upon him) had a ring made and wore it. He then said: ""This distracted me from you since today; a glance at it and a glance at you."" Then he threw it."
"3034","[AI-translation] From Fudalah bin 'Ubaid, marfu'an: ""Gray hair is light in the face of a Muslim, so whoever wishes may pluck his light."
"3035","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Gray hair is the light of a believer. No man grows a gray hair in Islam except that he gets a good deed for every gray hair and is raised a degree by it."
"3036","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The image is the head, so if the head is cut off, there is no image."
"3037","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw a jubbah lined with silk, so he said: ""A collar of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"3038","[AI-translation] Hanafiyyah, from his father, from his grandfather 'Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), marfu'an: ""Use antimony (ithmid), for it grows the hair, removes dirt, and clears the sight."
"3039","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Adhere to the siwak, for it purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"3040","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: ""Dye the gray hair and do not imitate the Jews or the Christians."
"3041","[AI-translation] From Usamah bin Zaid, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah in the Ka'bah, and he saw some images. He said: So he called for a bucket of water, I brought it to him, and he began erasing them, saying: ""May Allah fight a people who make images of what they do not create."
"3042","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: ""The most beloved of colors to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was green."
"3043","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), when he wore a turban, would let the ends of his turban hang between his shoulders."
"3044","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Samura who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) had white hairs in the front of his head and his beard. When he applied oil and combed it, they were not visible, but when his head was disheveled, they became visible. He had abundant hair and beard. A man asked, ""Was his face like a sword?"" He replied, ""No, rather it was like the sun and the moon, and it was round."" He said: ""And I saw his seal near his shoulder, like the egg of a dove, resembling his body."
"3045","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, elevated to the Prophet: His white hairs were about twenty in number."
"3046","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: There were pictures in the Ka'bah, so he ordered 'Umar bin Al-Khattab to erase them. 'Umar wet a cloth and erased them with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) then entered it, and there was nothing of them in it."
"3047","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Samura, and he mentioned the gray hairs of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), he said: There were some hairs in the parting of his head; when he oiled his head, they were not visible, and when he did not oil it, they became visible."
"3048","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: ""He had a cloak dyed with wars and saffron. He would go around with it among his wives. If it was the night of this one, she would sprinkle it with water; if it was the night of this one, she would sprinkle it with water; and if it was the night of this one, she would sprinkle it with water."
"3049","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah who said: The pillow upon which he slept at night was of leather, stuffed with palm fiber."
"3050","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Abd: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to order changing the gray hair, in opposition to the non-Arabs."
"3051","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to grant concession to women regarding leather socks."
"3052","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to apply kohl to his right eye three times, and his left eye two times."
"3053","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: ""He (peace be upon him and his family) used to apply kohl an odd number of times."
"3054","[AI-translation] Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd: ""He (peace be upon him and his family) used to frequently apply oil to his head and comb his beard with water."
"3055","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: ""He (peace be upon him and his family) used to wear a red cloak on the day of Eid."
"3056","[AI-translation] Narrated Uqbah bin Amir: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to prevent his family from wearing jewelry and silk, and would say: ""If you love the jewelry of Paradise and its silk, then do not wear them in this world."
"3057","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Shaqiq: A man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was a governor in Egypt. A man from his companions came to him and found him with unkempt hair and disheveled. He said: ""Why do I see you disheveled while you are a governor?"" He replied: ""He (peace be upon him and his family) used to forbid us from al-Irfah."" We said, ""And what is al-Irfah?"" He said: ""Combing the hair every day."
"3058","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whatever of the lower garment exceeds the two ankles is in the Fire."
"3059","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) raising it to the Prophet: ""May Allah curse the tattooers and those who get tattooed, (and those who attach hair extensions), those who pluck eyebrows, those who file their teeth for beauty, and those who change the creation of Allah."
"3060","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) cursed the one who tattoos the face."
"3061","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Darda': The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) met her one day and said: ""Where are you coming from, O Umm Darda'?"" She said: ""From the bathhouse."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: ""No woman removes her clothes outside her house except that she tears the veil between her and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"3062","[AI-translation] Juhani: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever abandons clothing out of humility for Allah while he is able to afford it, Allah will call him on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of creation, until He lets him choose from whichever garments of faith he wishes to wear."
"3063","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Whoever has hair, let him honor it."
"3064","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks from gold and silver vessels in this world will not drink from them in the Hereafter. Then he said: The clothing of the people of Paradise, the drink of the people of Paradise, and the vessels of the people of Paradise."
"3065","From Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays al-Juhanī: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Who will take care of Khālid ibn Nubayḥ?"" A man from Hudhayl, and he was at that time near ʿArafah at ʿArnah. ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays said: ""I will, O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me."" He said: ""When you see him, you will be awestruck by him."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I have never been awestruck by anything ever."" So ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays  set out until he reached the mountains of ʿArafah before the sun set. ʿAbdullāh said: ""I encountered a man and was terrified of him when I saw him, and I recognized him by the terror I felt that he was the one the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described."" He said to me: ""Who is the man?"" I said: ""A seeker of need; is there a place to spend the night?"" He said: ""Yes, so follow me."" He said: ""So I went in his tracks and prayed ʿAṣr two light rakʿahs, fearing that he might see me. Then I caught up with him and struck him with the sword. Then I departed and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him."" Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb said: ""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him a staff (mikhsarah) and said: 'Lean on this until you meet me, and few are those who lean on staffs.'"" Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb said: ""When ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays  died, he ordered that it be placed on his stomach and his shroud, and he was buried and it was buried with him."""
"3066","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace be upon him) while I had an izar that rustled. He said: ""Who is this?"" I said: ""Abdullah bin Umar."" He said: ""If you are Abdullah, then raise your izar."" So I raised my izar to the middle of the shanks, and his izar did not cease until he died."
"3067","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, marfu': The position of the izar is to the middle of the shanks and the calf; but if you refuse, then to below the shank, and the ankles have no right in the izar."
"3068","[AI-translation] Husayn, mursal: ""He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade that walls be covered."
"3069","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade that a man put on his shoes while standing."
"3070","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Mughaffal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade combing the hair except every other day."
"3071","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade the ring of gold and the ring of iron."
"3072","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Buraidah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""He (peace be upon him) forbade two sittings and two garments: As for the two sittings, it is sitting between the shade and the sun, and the other sitting is to wrap oneself in a garment that exposes one's Awrah. And the two garments: one of them is that you pray in a garment without wrapping it over your shoulders, and the other is that you pray in trousers without a Rida'."
"3073","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade Al-Mufaddam."
"3074","[AI-translation] From 'Imran bin Husain, marfu': He forbade the saddle-cushion of red leather."
"3075","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': I was forbidden from being naked. That was before prophethood was sent down upon him."
"3076","[AI-translation] From Khalid bin Ma'dan who said: Al-Miqdam bin Ma'di Karib came as a delegate to Mu'awiyah and said to him: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade the wearing of the skins of predators and riding upon them? He said: Yes."
"3077","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) went out to a group of the Ansar whose beards were white, and said: O gathering of the Ansar, dye red and yellow, and differ from the People of the Book. They said: O Messenger of Allah! The People of the Book cut their forelocks and let their mustaches grow. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Let your forelocks grow and shorten your mustaches, and differ from the People of the Book. They said: O Messenger of Allah! The People of the Book go barefoot and do not wear shoes. He said: Wear shoes and go barefoot, and differ from the People of the Book."
"3078","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her) and found a curtain at her door, so he did not enter. It was his practice that he would rarely enter without first visiting her. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) came and found her distressed, so he said: ""What is the matter with you?"" She said: ""The Prophet ﷺ came to me but did not enter."" So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Fāṭimah was greatly distressed that you came to her but did not enter upon her."" He said: ""What have I to do with the world? And what have I to do with embroidery?"" So he went to Fāṭimah and informed her of the Messenger of Allah's statement. She said: ""Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What does he command me to do?"" He said: ""Tell her: Let her send it to such-and-such a family."""
"3079","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah: From the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Woe to the women from the two reds: gold and safflower."
"3080","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik: That he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) with a gold ring on his hand one day, so the people rushed to rings. He threw it away and said: ""I will never wear it."
"3081","[AI-translation] Mughirah bin Shu'bah, marfu': O Sufyan bin Sahl, do not let your garment drag, for Allah does not love those who let their garments drag."
"3082","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn Fulān al-Anṣārī, who said: While he was walking with his lower garment trailing, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) caught up to him, having taken hold of his own forelock, saying: ""O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant."" ʿAmr said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am a man with thin shanks."" He said: ""O ʿAmr! Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has perfected everything He created. O ʿAmr!"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) struck with four fingers of his right hand below ʿAmr's knee, and said: ""O ʿAmr! This is the place of the lower garment."" Then he raised it and placed it below the other [knee] and said: ""O ʿAmr! This is the place of the lower garment."""
"3083","Thawban narrated: The daughter of Hubayrah came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while she had heavy gold rings on her hand. The Prophet (peace be upon him) began striking her hand. So she went to Fatimah to complain to her. Thawban said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) entered upon Fatimah while I was with him, and she had taken a gold necklace from around her neck. She said: ""This was gifted to me by Abu al-Hasan."" And there was a necklace in her hand. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah, would it please you if people said: 'Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad, has a necklace of fire on her hand?'"" So he left and did not sit. Fatimah then went to the necklace, sold it, bought a slave with its price, and freed her. When this reached the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: ""Praise be to Allah Who saved Fatimah from the Fire."""
